# Roadmap — build phases

Each phase ends with something **live and usable**, not a half-built everything. A phase is done only when its exit checks pass.

The prototype (`design/prototype/index.html`) is the spec for every screen. Open it in a browser and use it as the reference while building.

**Who does what:** 🧑‍💼 = owner (accounts, content, approvals), 🛠 = builder (you with Claude now, a developer after handover).

---

## B0 — Foundation ✅ (this commit)

What exists:
- Next.js 16 app with brand tokens, fonts, compressed images and a branded holding page.
- Waitlist sign-up (works as soon as Supabase keys are added) and an honest count (300 offline + online sign-ups).
- Database schema with row-level security for people, roles, audit log, waitlist, enquiries, confidential concerns, progress, corrections, products, batches, serials, orders, payments, gift cards, agreements and the investor area.
- Payment layer: Paystack, Flutterwave and bank transfer behind one interface; webhook signature checks; settlement rules; bank-only rule for shares and investments.
- Security headers, a gate for private areas, `/api/health`.
- 54 automated tests, including the real migrations run against Postgres. CI runs them on every push. The payment and security code was independently reviewed and every finding fixed.
- Docs: architecture, roadmap, data model, payments, security, content, handover.

Owner next steps 🧑‍💼 (see [OWNER-CHECKLIST.md](OWNER-CHECKLIST.md)): create the Supabase and Vercel projects, point `edenacres.ng` to Vercel, start Paystack and Flutterwave KYC now (it takes days).

**Exit check:** the holding page is live on edenacres.ng and a real waitlist sign-up lands in the database.

