## B1 — Public site (about 3–4 weeks)

Rebuild the prototype's public pages as real pages, with the content in data files so text can be edited without touching layout.

- Home, About, Estate (zones), Farm and produce brands, Dairy, Equestrian and racing, Stays and events (enquiry only), Farmers programme, Progress (live from the database), Trust and transparency (promises, status board, corrections log), Contact, FAQ, Privacy, Terms.
- Shop catalogue in **browse-only** mode: product pages, "Pre-order soon" and "Coming soon" badges, no payment yet.
- Product verification page `/verify` and trace page `/trace` (server route with rate limit and PIN HMAC).
- Forms: contact and enquiries, farmer applications, confidential concerns (with receipt code), counterfeit reports.
- "Ask Eden" assistant, answering only from an approved facts file, with "I don't know, ask the team" fallback.
- Three languages (English, Yorùbá, Naijá), with professional review of Yorùbá before launch.
- SEO (metadata, sitemap, Open Graph images), analytics (privacy-friendly), Sentry, Content Security Policy, rate limiting on every public form, cookie notice if analytics needs one.
- Accessibility pass (keyboard, contrast, alt text) and mobile pass against the prototype's mobile screens.

**Exit check:** all public pages match the prototype on desktop and mobile; Lighthouse ≥ 90 for performance, accessibility and SEO; every form stores to the database and emails the team.

